    "checks": [
      "D_b is the precision pushforward of k=floor(d/n) independent same-sign component-Haar matrices; the precision contains the canonical affine symmetric blocks and an untouched d mod n identity tail.",
      "The primitive plan asks O_j and its transpose on each corresponding input block. Its decoder returns the true potential value and derivative-based gradient of the symmetric quadratic at the requested point.",
      "A measured independent seed starts an arbitrary Borel state machine, including the complete-history constructor. Actual early stopping and the terminal readout of the final allowed response are both represented. The per-block cost equals twice the number of executed first-order queries, uniformly over each seed and matrix tuple.",
      "The public statement has only the source numeric hypotheses plus an algorithm and seed probability and takes bind over precision inputs of the fixed-input output law. The seed is averaged with a product prior. The required maps and kernels are measurable.",
      "For d=11,n=5,k=2,T=2,kappa=4 an independent uniform Boolean seed selects a one-query or a two-query run. The second point is gradient plus value times first point, and the readout retains both seed information and terminal response. The first point uses the identity tail. The consumer obtains both exact path outputs for all fixed matrices and the final equality from the published theorem.",
      "The general supplemental test proves that each prior-averaged output is a probability measure for both supported signs, every probability seed law, and every such algorithm."
    ]
